            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for the schedule, then the German for to change your plans."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: unvorhergesehen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "unvorhergesehen — \"unforeseen, unexpected\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Wegen eines unvorhergesehenen Problems kommt der Techniker erst morgen. Because of an unforeseen problem the technician is not coming until tomorrow."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Built from un-, vorher — beforehand — and gesehen — seen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "unvorhergesehen is built from un- \"not\", vorher \"beforehand\" and gesehen, the participle of sehen \"to see\", Old High German sehan (EtymDB): not seen in advance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
