          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "berücksichtigen — \"to take into account\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Bei der Reise müssen wir auch das Wetter berücksichtigen. For the trip we also have to take the weather into account."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Inseparable: er berücksichtigt, er hat berücksichtigt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "berücksichtigen is built on Rücksicht \"consideration\", literally a looking back, from Rücken \"back\" and Sicht \"sight\", of the family of sehen (EtymDB). Rücksicht is usually explained as a rendering of Latin respectus \"a looking back\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
